  "notes": [
    "पसंद है works the other way round from English. The thing liked is the subject, and the person takes को: मुझे (= मुझको) चाय पसंद है is \"to me, tea is liked\".",
    "With a plural thing, है becomes हैं: मुझे आम पसंद हैं (I like mangoes).",
    "पसंदीदा (favourite) is common but a little formal. सबसे ज़्यादा पसंद (\"liked most of all\") is just as natural."
  ]
